row-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know about you guys, but these alien spirits that hitch rides on meteorites are giving me WAAAAY too many ideas. I wonder what a spirit from Saturn's hexagon would look like....</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I thought they were cooler than the Idigam. But then, I am kind of a sucker for stuff like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-23-2014, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T14:26:20-07:00","id":147157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=147148#post147148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, I thought they were cooler than the Idigam. But then, I am kind of a sucker for stuff like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kinda thought the same way too. I'm more interested in seeing what I could do with a Spirit who is supposed to exist but isn't like anything we've encountered before so it upsets the Shadow's structure, the human population and just how things work in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T14:29:13-07:00","id":147159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=147139#post147139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know about you guys, but these alien spirits that hitch rides on meteorites are giving me WAAAAY too many ideas. I wonder what a spirit from Saturn's hexagon would look like....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Spirits from outside lunar orbit? Huh. Funny you should mention that...<br /> <br /> Oh, on an entirely unrelated topic: those idigam that Stew mentioned in the blog post? Part of what I did on the book was to write a few of those. I'm quite keen on folks to see them, and I hope they are well-received! (By Storytellers anyway. Players, on the other hand....) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T14:32:51-07:00","id":147162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=147138#post147138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stew says they're spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No he doesn't","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","name":"Furry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T14:42:46-07:00","id":147166,"title":"","content":"Ok, now you are just trolling.<br /> <br /> For the record (and this appears in the blog linked in the OP):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Idigam Chronicles' Setting Bible</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idigam are creatures from before time, <i><u><b>spirits</b></u></i> of concepts that do not \u2014 can not \u2014 exist in the world as we know it</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T14:52:24-07:00","id":147182,"title":"","content":"The Fenric comparison right on the heels of &quot;they're not cosmic horrors&quot; gives me ample cause to believe Stew when he says that he's sleep-deprived; I can't help but look at the latter as an excuse to talk shit about Lovecraft, which, while not unreasonable, is kind of off-subject. They're ancient shifting monstrosities from before history that truck with mysterious beings from beyond the stars and that's generally enough to ping most people's understanding of the popcultural version of Lovecraft.<br /> <br /> Certainly looking forward to seeing if members of the Celestial Courts besides Lunes and Helions are hanging around the setting; that's a thing I've been curious about since the corebook mentioned them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T15:01:05-07:00","id":147188,"title":"","content":"First off, let me say that I was listening to <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l35oH3BoRGU\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> (Revenge by Aviators) while I was reading. It makes more sense, really, despite being based off of a certain popular children's animated series.<br /> <br /> So, let me see if I got this straight: Impossible spirits who must change to have any anchorage in reality who urge, ride, and <i>claim</i> other spirits and assemble courts of the spirits of celestial bodies who are out to make the bastards/bitches pay for their imprisonment by taking it out on their world and particularly their children.<br /> <br /> I can see one such court after claiming humanity, and they are <i>awesome</i>.<br /> <br /> I thought nothing of these guys before, now I love them. I particularly like the fact they make packs with star spirits-I like any invocations of stars, really, so that just makes me happy.<br /> <br /> Which isn't to say something the Idigam themselves aren't interesting. Oh damn, the images in my mind, I love them and am terrified of them. These guys are cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T15:01:09-07:00","id":147189,"title":"","content":"Nothing you didn't got if you read Wolfbane. Color me disappointed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T15:23:28-07:00","id":147208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=147159#post147159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirits from outside lunar orbit? Huh. Funny you should mention that...<br /> <br /> Oh, on an entirely unrelated topic: those idigam that Stew mentioned in the blog post? Part of what I did on the book was to write a few of those. I'm quite keen on folks to see them, and I hope they are well-received! (By Storytellers anyway. Players, on the other hand....) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ....<br /> <br /> Please tell me we are going to see intergalactic spirits.<br /> <br /> PLEASE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T15:56:37-07:00","id":147242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=147208#post147208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> ....<br /> <br /> Please tell me we are going to see intergalactic spirits.<br /> <br /> PLEASE.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If I confirm or deny anything for sure, I think Stew might punch me or something. Or have someone else do it.<br /> <br /> But I may have taken some inspiration for one of the idigam that you may enjoy. That's all I'll say. (The idigam itself though is definitely NOT intergalactic, let me point that out right now.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T16:32:11-07:00","id":147271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=147242#post147242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I confirm or deny anything for sure, I think Stew might punch me or something. Or have someone else do it.<br /> <br /> But I may have taken some inspiration for one of the idigam that you may enjoy. That's all I'll say. (The idigam itself though is definitely NOT intergalactic, let me point that out right now.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell Stew I shall counter that argument by translating every single term you need translated into First Tongue, and I'll do it in a week, for spoilers.<br /> <br /> (It's the best deal I can offer.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T17:05:30-07:00","id":147292,"title":"","content":"Reading this thread before the blog, I was thinking they used 'spirit' as a generic term for an ephemeral entity not of this world. Now it seems clear the Idigam are either 1) spirits of concepts that are irrelevant now, or once existed but not anymore or 2) spirits of far, distant places well beyond the influence of Earth","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T18:09:11-07:00","id":147387,"title":"","content":"In Vampire's Ancient Bloodlines/Mysteries, a long time ago En Isiratuu was, effectively, the king of the vampires in his area, ruling for thousands of years, diablerizing without much worry of loss, stealing powers and skills left and right, and overall being an unstoppable jerk. Some members of the Circle of the Crone (a different cult back then, but with Cruac) summoned spirits from distant stars, binding them into a body (I forget if it's a vampire or a regular person, but it ended up being vampiric, at least). Its eyes glowed with the light of far off stars, and it had powers few vampires could recognize. En Isiratuu, despite having some warning beforehand about a mysterious warrior who would defeat him, confronted the thing and wanted its power. Unfortunately for him, part of its power rested in diablerie, and its ability to lure vampires to commit it. Upon committing diablerie on the creature, the Edimmu, the spirits multiplied within En Isiratuu, exploding outward, killing him, and seven groups of the spirits (there were seven spirits, but when they 'bred' they had seven offspring) sought out the nearest other vampires and possessed them, who lured other vampires to commit diablerie, then multiplied, and so forth.<br /> <br /> That is one of the theories as to why the ban against diablerie is one of the traditions, as although many of the things were bound, it was difficult to do so (requiring the investigation of and taking advantage of seven different bans for each Edimmu), and theoretically they're still out there, waiting for some enterprising person to unwrap a gold chain around a corpse's leg or something.<br /> <br /> I always liked them.<br /> <br /> So...color me excited for more spirits from beyond Earth and our solar system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T18:37:39-07:00","id":147402,"title":"","content":"Guys, I just said I took inspiration from such an idea, <b>not</b> that such spirits were in the book. Just being clear, there.<br /> <br /> I think, though, that the basic spirit rules in GMC are enough to start from in order for a Storyteller so inclined to build those kinds of spirits for themselves, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T18:43:43-07:00","id":147406,"title":"","content":"Oh I wasn't suggesting that, just like the idea of spirits from outer space. Whether written up in the book by you or other writers or not, we've got some nods to use that kind of thing. Considering Werewolf already has a vast rogues gallery, of sorts, this just expands it even further.<br /> <br /> Spirits of black holes and nebulae and the cold void of space, of planets and moons and stars that haven't even been seen by man. And then it opens up the possibilities of claimed and ridden of these things, or cults worshiping them if they've managed to wander away from their idigam summoners, or still working with them. Outside of the Mirrors books, World of Darkness has very little outer space stuff, until now. If you go so far as to decide there's aliens and alien life out there, you have alien spaceship spirits and spirits of alien lifeforms and alien concepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-23-2014, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T19:34:38-07:00","id":147460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=147406#post147406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh I wasn't suggesting that, just like the idea of spirits from outer space. Whether written up in the book by you or other writers or not, we've got some nods to use that kind of thing. Considering Werewolf already has a vast rogues gallery, of sorts, this just expands it even further.<br /> <br /> Spirits of black holes and nebulae and the cold void of space, of planets and moons and stars that haven't even been seen by man. And then it opens up the possibilities of claimed and ridden of these things, or cults worshiping them if they've managed to wander away from their idigam summoners, or still working with them. Outside of the Mirrors books, World of Darkness has very little outer space stuff, until now. If you go so far as to decide there's aliens and alien life out there, you have alien spaceship spirits and spirits of alien lifeforms and alien concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And we just discovered a wormhole at our Milky Way's center.<br /> <br /> Try to wrap your head around THAT.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T21:28:46-07:00","id":147544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=147460#post147460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And we just discovered a wormhole at our Milky Way's center. Try to wrap your head around THAT.</div> </div> </div> </div> ...source please? From what I've read, wormholes at the centers of galaxies would be nearly indistinguishable from supermassive black holes (which current theory holds are at the center of every galaxy). Recently a way was discovered to determine the difference, but I had not heard that Sagittarius A* had been confirmed one or the other yet. In fact, last I heard it wouldn't be possible to tell until the next generation of orbital telescopes, so at least a few years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T22:52:37-07:00","id":147632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=147544#post147544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ...source please? From what I've read, wormholes at the centers of galaxies would be nearly indistinguishable from supermassive black holes (which current theory holds are at the center of every galaxy). Recently a way was discovered to determine the difference, but I had not heard that Sagittarius A* had been confirmed one or the other yet. In fact, last I heard it wouldn't be possible to tell until the next generation of orbital telescopes, so at least a few years.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://medium.com/the-physics-arxiv-blog/bb5ae64fa4fa\" target=\"_blank\">https://medium.com/the-physics-arxiv-blog/bb5ae64fa4fa</a><br /> <br /> I've likely misread the article, though, so thank you for pointing that out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T00:02:52-07:00","id":147684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=147406#post147406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirits of black holes and nebulae and the cold void of space, of planets and moons and stars that haven't even been seen by man. And then it opens up the possibilities of claimed and ridden of these things, or cults worshiping them if they've managed to wander away from their idigam summoners, or still working with them. Outside of the Mirrors books, World of Darkness has very little outer space stuff, until now. If you go so far as to decide there's aliens and alien life out there, you have alien spaceship spirits and spirits of alien lifeforms and alien concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Luna/Moon and Sol/Sunna are spirits of Rank 8, what would be those? I assume that stars, planets and moons would be all Rank 8 by this, but nebulas and galaxies should be there be Rank 9. And then logical is that whole cosmos and creation would be Ain Soph of Rank 10. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm eager to see Mars or Venus spirits making guest visits to werewolves and mages from time to time... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T00:05:10-07:00","id":147685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=147182#post147182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Fenric comparison right on the heels of &quot;they're not cosmic horrors&quot; gives me ample cause to believe Stew when he says that he's sleep-deprived; I can't help but look at the latter as an excuse to talk shit about Lovecraft, which, while not unreasonable, is kind of off-subject. They're ancient shifting monstrosities from before history that truck with mysterious beings from beyond the stars and that's generally enough to ping most people's understanding of the popcultural version of Lovecraft.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally agree - half of post is to mark that Idigams aren't Lovecraftian horrors, but describing it as it technically was one.<br /> <br /> And I feel here a strong <b>Mage</b> crossover potential...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T00:59:48-07:00","id":147723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=147684#post147684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If Luna/Moon and Sol/Sunna are spirits of Rank 8, what would be those? I assume that stars, planets and moons would be all Rank 8 by this, but nebulas and galaxies should be there be Rank 9. And then logical is that whole cosmos and creation would be Ain Soph of Rank 10. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm eager to see Mars or Venus spirits making guest visits to werewolves and mages from time to time... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The books point out that Luna and Helios are not necessarily 8, they may be 9, and no one knows exactly which, it's a matter of debate among the people who know (just like it is on the boards).<br /> <br /> That said, the sun and the moon have been worshiped or at least been in a place of importance for many religions, and the sun and the moon have influenced the world for millions of years before humanity was around to name them. The fact that nebulae are large doesn't necessarily make them more powerful (or Helios would be more powerful than Gaia and Luna combined), though they may be up there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-24-2014, 04:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T04:30:30-07:00","id":147768,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I would think a spirit of Mars would have a higher rank than a spirit of Mercury just because Mars has more of an influence on humanity's dreams and thoughts, you know? I think rank 7 would be the bare minimum for any spirit representing a stellar or cosmic body","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T04:43:24-07:00","id":147770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=147406#post147406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh I wasn't suggesting that, just like the idea of spirits from outer space. Whether written up in the book by you or other writers or not, we've got some nods to use that kind of thing. Considering Werewolf already has a vast rogues gallery, of sorts, this just expands it even further.<br /> <br /> Spirits of black holes and nebulae and the cold void of space, of planets and moons and stars that haven't even been seen by man. And then it opens up the possibilities of claimed and ridden of these things, or cults worshiping them if they've managed to wander away from their idigam summoners, or still working with them. Outside of the Mirrors books, World of Darkness has very little outer space stuff, until now. If you go so far as to decide there's aliens and alien life out there, you have alien spaceship spirits and spirits of alien lifeforms and alien concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, there's been no real change. A Storyteller who wanted to could have easily inserted some sort of extraterrestrial spirit if they were so inclined. I'd suggest that doing so is a bit out-of-theme for Werewolf if going by the Father Wolf story, but that doesn't stop Storytellers from putting them in if they like. Really, they'd just use the same spirit rules as everything else. The thing to remember is that, theoretically, there's potentially a spirit out there for <i>anything</i>. What a Storyteller does with that is up to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T06:46:42-07:00","id":147810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=147770#post147770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, there's been no real change. A Storyteller who wanted to could have easily inserted some sort of extraterrestrial spirit if they were so inclined. I'd suggest that doing so is a bit out-of-theme for Werewolf if going by the Father Wolf story, but that doesn't stop Storytellers from putting them in if they like. Really, they'd just use the same spirit rules as everything else. The thing to remember is that, theoretically, there's potentially a spirit out there for <i>anything</i>. What a Storyteller does with that is up to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>wait wait wait! are you telling me there is a spirit of Doritos running around?! Also, is there a much more specific spirit of the spirit of starving college students who eat nothing but cup ramen all day?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T07:00:06-07:00","id":147818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=147810#post147810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> wait wait wait! are you telling me there is a spirit of Doritos running around?! Also, is there a much more specific spirit of the spirit of starving college students who eat nothing but cup ramen all day?</div> </div> </div> </div> Maybe not quite that specific, but I could imagine a spirit of academia hanging out on a college campus, devouring hunger spirits, ramen spirits, etc. and gaining those as influences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T07:25:36-07:00","id":147829,"title":"","content":"I was just thinking about this last night. I don't think you'd find Dorito spirits anywhere but where the brand was very important. A vending machine or snack aisle would probably have ambiguous snack spirits, but at a Doritos factory or their company HQ you'd probably have some spirit brands (ha ha). Even other places, spirits might be subtly influenced, soda spirits having a red wrapping or what have you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-24-2014, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T08:20:57-07:00","id":147846,"title":"","content":"If Luna is a rank 8/9 spirit then the idigam that could destroy her is either a higher rank or know her ban, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T10:08:19-07:00","id":147917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=147846#post147846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Luna is a rank 8/9 spirit then the idigam that could destroy her is either a higher rank or know her ban, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>What makes you think Idigam could destroy Her?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 05-24-2014, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T11:15:52-07:00","id":147978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=147846#post147846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Luna is a rank 8/9 spirit then the idigam that could destroy her is either a higher rank or know her ban, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying it wouldn't be possible if that's what you'd want in your campaign, but remember the Idigam (most but not all...?) were <b>imprisoned on the moon</b>. Had they been able to defeat Luna somehow, it would've taken a lot of knowledge and power. The best they could do is sneak out when she wasn't looking. But yeah, I would assume like anything else as long as they have the tricks and strength to do so then why not?<br /> <br /> Wouldn't Luna's death have some implications on the Forsaken's relationship to the moon, though? Auspice gifts and shapeshifting and such? That's what would really matter","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T13:38:29-07:00","id":148089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=147846#post147846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Luna is a rank 8/9 spirit then the idigam that could destroy her is either a higher rank or know her ban, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe there's been mention of an idigam that could destroy her, they seem mostly interested in destroying werewolves.<br /> <br /> In Wolfsbane, the idigam we've been given are mostly spirit rank 5, with a couple at 4.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=147978#post147978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't Luna's death have some implications on the Forsaken's relationship to the moon, though? Auspice gifts and shapeshifting and such? That's what would really matter</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. No more lunacy or auspices, no more lunes watching out.<br /> I don't believe they'd lose their shapeshifting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-24-2014, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T14:06:28-07:00","id":148108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=147189#post147189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing you didn't got if you read Wolfbane. Color me disappointed.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I've been voting for other things, especially when Lodges is one of the choices. Stew mentioned in a previous blog that Lodges didn't really change much at all, so I have no desire to see that when something else that has a greater impact on the core game itself is an option to review.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T14:25:33-07:00","id":148134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amaterasu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=148108#post148108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is why I've been voting for other things, especially when Lodges is one of the choices. Stew mentioned in a previous blog that Lodges didn't really change much at all, so I have no desire to see that when something else that has a greater impact on the core game itself is an option to review.</div> </div> </div> </div>I voted Lodges because I saw this coming a mile away.<br /> <br /> Really subpar previews as a whole if you compare them with the ones done for B&amp;S. Why? Because it's not the writers who do the spoilers, and raise hype on them. Who have actual time to reply to us, address our concerns, and do some revision right there.<br /> <br /> NVM Stew got at least two projects to juggle, counting IC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T00:03:52-07:00","id":148447,"title":"","content":"I think B&amp;S was more &quot;throwing things out to get fans to playtest&quot; while this is more &quot;showing things off for review and fan hype&quot; rather than the former. Not that I expect to get a full list of all the gifts or something, but I understand what you mean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T05:54:46-07:00","id":148636,"title":"","content":"You guys know that lodge of last winter I've been harping about? Long buried idigam that when raised destroys luna. All werewolves essentially become pure. Even has a small blurb about playing in a post apocalyptic world. Tribes if the moon, storm lord section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T06:47:33-07:00","id":148670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=148636#post148636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You guys know that lodge of last winter I've been harping about? Long buried idigam that when raised destroys luna. All werewolves essentially become pure. Even has a small blurb about playing in a post apocalyptic world. Tribes if the moon, storm lord section.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no metaplot, just sayin'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T07:51:28-07:00","id":148697,"title":"","content":"You guys doubted any claims of an idigam being that powerful. Meta plot or no there is an example right there. And it wasn't moon banished from what I can tell. Just deep slumbering","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T08:01:23-07:00","id":148698,"title":"","content":"For all of your post apocalyptic needs, I will just link this here. Possibly the best book ever from the gameline <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/1619/Apocalypse?cPath=6536&amp;it=1\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/produc...Path=6536&amp;it=1</a><br /> <br /> What makes it better is since it is mostly plot involved, it doesn't suffer from import issues to Forsaken provided your plot is moving towards this path already","signature":"","edited":{"userid":444,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","user":"Dessembrae","date":". 05-25-2014, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T09:43:15-07:00","id":148745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=148698#post148698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For all of your post apocalyptic needs, I will just link this here. Possibly the best book ever from the gameline <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/1619/Apocalypse?cPath=6536&amp;it=1\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/produc...Path=6536&amp;it=1</a><br /> <br /> What makes it better is since it is mostly plot involved, it doesn't suffer from import issues to Forsaken provided your plot is moving towards this path already</div> </div> </div> </div>one of the scenarios can easily be added to the forsaken line<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=148697#post148697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You guys doubted any claims of an idigam being that powerful. Meta plot or no there is an example right there. And it wasn't moon banished from what I can tell. Just deep slumbering</div> </div> </div> </div>Idigams are a dark unknown thing , if luna bound them then they cannot defeat her , though what if they managed somehow to cooperate in order to do so , OR make humankind take part in that scheme ? Evangelion esque , baka suthar anzuth , baka mennina !! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2194,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","user":"Furry","date":". 05-25-2014, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","name":"Furry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T10:09:42-07:00","id":148759,"title":"","content":"-shudders- I hate Eva. It isn't deep or profound, it's just badly or not at all explained. Everyone loves it though o.O. As for the idigam, I love the idea of a deep sleeping beast. I was hoping it'd get a write up but that's not to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T11:02:04-07:00","id":148794,"title":"","content":"Op I misspoke, the idigam in question CAN be contained within the moon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T11:47:09-07:00","id":149580,"title":"","content":"There doesn't seem to be much that is particularly new about the Idigam; but the idea of a pack facing a creature that even Father Wolf couldn't kill is still an interesting one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T11:58:08-07:00","id":149609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=148759#post148759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-shudders- I hate Eva. It isn't deep or profound, it's just badly or not at all explained. Everyone loves it though o.O. As for the idigam, I love the idea of a deep sleeping beast. I was hoping it'd get a write up but that's not to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hideaki Ano has a lot of issues that he showcases with his baby, but undoubtedly the biggest problem of it is is that the philosophy Ano was exploring was a troublesome idea for an anime, and he played it completely straight, Add in his bad handling of depression and the studio's general problems with financial handling and Eva kind of just crashes on it's whole. The first two thirds are solid enough though as a smarter mecha genre series, and watching the effect Eva has on viewers(and especially <i>fans</i>) is really interesting. I still hate it, but credit where credit is due.<br /> <br /> IDIGAM! Actually, I like the smaller but more active Idigam. Giant sleeping beasts beyond or under reality is cool and all, but it's not the sort of thing I want to throw into many chronicles. The Idigam have a neat strix like ability to help move things behind the scenes or to be an upfront antagonist, and as such I can get a lot more use out of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T07:33:24-07:00","id":150321,"title":"","content":"So...... I'm at a loss with the Idigam. The writers say they're not Lovcraftian beings... but are pretty much described like one to me. They've been consistently referred to as spirits time and again, yet we're told that they're NOT spirits, since the Bone Shadows don't specialize in hunting them. <br /> <br /> What gives? I'm getting a very strong vibe of &quot;The writer doth protest too much, me thinks.&quot; Okay, so we're talking about primordial and/or rival celestial (read: not Lunar/Solar) spirits. They're in flux with difficult-to-get-bans. Okay. What is there about them that makes them special enough to be a titular aspect of the game? How is it encompassing werewolf-hood?<br /> <br /> The strix are the darkest parts of vampires, all the hunger without any restraining Man, a mirror darkly. Angels have a strong thematic tie to demons, their reflection and who they once were. Both speak strongly to the game's core themes. <br /> <br /> What is there about Idigam that makes it so special or important to Werewolf? I'm not feeling it. Sure, you can make a cool antagonist. But... is that it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T07:50:51-07:00","id":150333,"title":"","content":"The beings of Lovecraft represent his philosophical theories about cosmicism, which suggest that, among other things, if there are beings of great power and knowledge out there, they don't care a whit about humanity, as humanity is insignificant in the grand scheme of the universe.<br /> <br /> The idigam, however, really are interested in the Forsaken (not sure if it's werewolves as a whole), because they hate them. They hate them so much. <br /> <br /> They are spirits. They are just a very special kind of spirit. They aren't one of the sacred prey because they're so rare, not because they're not spirits, and they have powers that, due to their nature, don't conform to the standard rules people know about spirits. It's the kind of confrontation that's going to involve thinking outside of the standard mindset, like hunting a vampire when you're prepared to hunt humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-27-2014, 10:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T10:23:02-07:00","id":150503,"title":"","content":"As I understand it, they were the first spirits. Born of the chaos of the still-forming universe (personally, I change that to the still-forming earth in my own games to make them a bit less cosmic and to justify their canonically lower rank than a lot of younger and more local spirits). They represent concepts that no longer exist, so their nature is fundamentally different from that of modern spirits. I think they're the central antagonists of the chronicle for a couple of reasons. For one thing, they're super powerful and damn hard to kill, which makes them convenient big bads. They also give ST's an easy way to tie the Idigam chronicle into the God Machine Chronicle and DtD if you're into that kind of crossover, by having their lunar prison be the tomb of the butterfly. But I think most importantly, they are antagonistic to the very nature of werewolves. The Wolf Must Hunt, and the Idigam are the one thing The Wolf Can't Hunt. Even Urfarah had to accept that they were just too inconstant for him to kill, and his only option was to imprison them. Now they're back, they have even more reason to hate you than other spirits, and they're as impossible to kill as ever. They're the out-of-context problem, the one you can't solve by your normal methods. You can't just hunt them, you have to find a way to trick them into coalescing, into accepting the rules of a constant, ordered universe and gaining a Ban, and only then can they be killed. Vampire is a game about internal struggle with your monsterous nature, and the Strix are an external representation of that internal struggle. Werewolf is a game about the need to hunt, and the Idigam as a thing-you-can't-hunt are a representation of your own shortcomings. They're living proof that you are not the perfect hunter you believe yourself to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T10:58:27-07:00","id":150589,"title":"","co