"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T08:13:34-07:00","id":151312,"title":"","content":"Something we can say about the ancient monsters facet of the Idigam is that during ancient times, after Urfarah imprisoned them, but thousands of years before the moon-landing, they may have inspired the legends of mythological monsters. There's scores of mythological creatures to inspire ourselves with to craft our own. Tartaros, Echidna, Typhon, Kraken, Ancalagon, etc, etc, etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T11:42:22-07:00","id":151532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=150503#post150503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I understand it, they were the first spirits. Born of the chaos of the still-forming universe (personally, I change that to the still-forming earth in my own games to make them a bit less cosmic and to justify their canonically lower rank than a lot of younger and more local spirits). They represent concepts that no longer exist, so their nature is fundamentally different from that of modern spirits. I think they're the central antagonists of the chronicle for a couple of reasons. For one thing, they're super powerful and damn hard to kill, which makes them convenient big bads. They also give ST's an easy way to tie the Idigam chronicle into the God Machine Chronicle and DtD if you're into that kind of crossover, by having their lunar prison be the tomb of the butterfly. But I think most importantly, they are antagonistic to the very nature of werewolves. The Wolf Must Hunt, and the Idigam are the one thing The Wolf Can't Hunt. Even Urfarah had to accept that they were just too inconstant for him to kill, and his only option was to imprison them. Now they're back, they have even more reason to hate you than other spirits, and they're as impossible to kill as ever. They're the out-of-context problem, the one you can't solve by your normal methods. You can't just hunt them, you have to find a way to trick them into coalescing, into accepting the rules of a constant, ordered universe and gaining a Ban, and only then can they be killed. Vampire is a game about internal struggle with your monsterous nature, and the Strix are an external representation of that internal struggle. Werewolf is a game about the need to hunt, and the Idigam as a thing-you-can't-hunt are a representation of your own shortcomings. They're living proof that you are not the perfect hunter you believe yourself to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciate your explanation, and it gives logic for this decision. None the less, Idigam aren't thing I would connect to game called <b>Werewolf </b>as antagonist. Strix are darker mirror of Kindred, they are ephemeral vampires. Idigam are... what to the werewolves? No analogy in main antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T12:56:36-07:00","id":151605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=151532#post151532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I appreciate your explanation, and it gives logic for this decision. None the less, Idigam aren't thing I would connect to game called <b>Werewolf </b>as antagonist. Strix are darker mirror of Kindred, they are ephemeral vampires. Idigam are... what to the werewolves? No analogy in main antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lemme summarize the above in a single sentence:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i><b>The Wolf Must Hunt, and the Idigam are the one thing The Wolf Can't Hunt.</b> </i> </div> </div> </div>You need dark reflections of the protagonists? that's what the Pure are for. You need <i>Twisted</i> reflections of the protagonists? Unihar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T13:06:37-07:00","id":151615,"title":"","content":"It is worth noting, though, that there is still a foil quality to the Idigam.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are creatures defined by their shapeshifting, driven by their rage, supported by a celestial body, and enact several unusual powers that spring from their unique nature.<br /> <br /> Idigam are perpetually shifting creatures driven by their hatred who tend to get the help of celestial bodies and enact several unusual powers that spring from their unique nature.<br /> <br /> Which makes them <i>awesome.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T16:00:41-07:00","id":151787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=151532#post151532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I appreciate your explanation, and it gives logic for this decision. None the less, Idigam aren't thing I would connect to game called <b>Werewolf </b>as antagonist. Strix are darker mirror of Kindred, they are ephemeral vampires. Idigam are... what to the werewolves? No analogy in main antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of the point. The games have different themes, so they have to have different challenges. The Strix neeed to be deeply connected to the Kindred because Requiem is such an internally focused game; the primary conflict is a struggle against yourself, and the Strix are the worst parts of yourself. The Idigam need to be entirely alien to the Uratha in order to oppose them on the same level the Strix oppose vampires. Werewolves are the apex predator within their frame of reference, so their ultimate antagonist could only be something from outside that frame of reference. They're such a threat specifically <b>because</b> they have no analogue within werewolves' experience. And the only way you can beat them is by forcing them into a context you have experience with, forcing them to accept a Ban.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T18:04:00-07:00","id":151879,"title":"","content":"But Ephsy, aren't the ancient ones mentioned in predators more likely to be those mythological entities?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T18:13:23-07:00","id":151883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=151879#post151879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Ephsy, aren't the ancient ones mentioned in predators more likely to be those mythological entities?</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://24.media.tumblr.com/c4b8f12016e305d4b6d36ae8d7c5d3af/tumblr_mkws36UgVu1ry10fwo1_400.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T18:23:03-07:00","id":151895,"title":"","content":"Speaking of which, I believe one of the origin stories for the nosferatu dovetails with the Zmai from Predators. The Brothers Worm coterie who delved into the dark heart of the earth and ate the immaculate slime of the writhing god that lived there.<br /> <br /> I suppose another way to look at the Idigam, though it probably wouldn't satisfy, would be to point out that, as spirit cops (or spirit slashers), following in the footsteps of Father Wolf, they've had it relatively easy. The Pure are always there, but sometimes they're less of a threat and in the end they're wolves like you, not necessarily disrupting the Gauntlet. Spirits certainly don't like you (I always viewed this as the common man vs the police, rather than outright hatred, there's usually an unspoken intimidation that these guys with guns who consider themselves the authority carry around with them, if that makes any sense), but spirits spirit and you don't often have to go to all out war with them, sometimes their rises and falls in power are entirely natural. Urged and claimed are rarities. The shartha are certainly tough, but they're nothing compared to the Plague King and the Spinner-hag.<br /> <br /> But the idigam were something even Father Wolf couldn't defeat. And I doubt there's many Uratha who have the access to get one to the moon. So long ago the First Pack saw Father Wolf weakening and thought they'd do the right thing and take up his mantle. The world hasn't been enveloped in the Shadow, so they've done well enough. But the idigam are back and are going to be the true test of their worth, the greatest challenge they'll ever face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-28-2014, 10:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T21:31:07-07:00","id":152091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=151615#post151615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is worth noting, though, that there is still a foil quality to the Idigam.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are creatures defined by their shapeshifting, driven by their rage, supported by a celestial body, and enact several unusual powers that spring from their unique nature.<br /> <br /> Idigam are perpetually shifting creatures driven by their hatred who tend to get the help of celestial bodies and enact several unusual powers that spring from their unique nature.<br /> <br /> Which makes them <i>awesome.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Totally agree, and now I'm bought on &quot;Idigam are twisted dark mirror to Uratha as a species&quot;. Maybe corellation is more vauge as in Strix vs Kindred, but very suitable.<br /> <br /> And I alwyas wanted to put players against Azathoth as big bad in WoD chronicle. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-31-2014, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T03:32:22-07:00","id":152303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=151895#post151895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose another way to look at the Idigam, though it probably wouldn't satisfy, would be to point out that, as spirit cops (or spirit slashers), following in the footsteps of Father Wolf, they've had it relatively easy. The Pure are always there, but sometimes they're less of a threat and in the end they're wolves like you, not necessarily disrupting the Gauntlet. Spirits certainly don't like you (I always viewed this as the common man vs the police, rather than outright hatred, there's usually an unspoken intimidation that these guys with guns who consider themselves the authority carry around with them, if that makes any sense), but spirits spirit and you don't often have to go to all out war with them, sometimes their rises and falls in power are entirely natural. Urged and claimed are rarities. The shartha are certainly tough, but they're nothing compared to the Plague King and the Spinner-hag.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just gonna point out that the only ones who would be &quot;spirit cops&quot; are gonna be the Bone Shadows, and that's not the imagery they convey at all.<br /> <br /> Are we gonna refer to Blood Talons (Lodge besides) as Uratha cops? How about the Meninna? Sharta cops?<br /> <br /> That's the genius of assigning each tribe a favored prey, IMO.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T11:22:27-07:00","id":152722,"title":"","content":"I guess it'll depend on the 'why' of the spirit hunt. Are they just picking people at random, or are they picking targets that upset the Shadow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T21:24:14-07:00","id":153481,"title":"","content":"The Storm Lords are absolutely spirit cops, too. I see them as more of that archetype than the Shadows, in fact. And you could argue that that is the root of the Meninna's hunt, too - the Hosts upset the balance between the Shadow and the material world, and the Beshilu in particular give spirits an easy entrance into the world. Hell, as nofather said, you can easily say that the Iron Masters hunt humans *because* of their effect on the Shadow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T02:28:04-07:00","id":153625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NateD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=153481#post153481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Storm Lords are absolutely spirit cops, too. I see them as more of that archetype than the Shadows, in fact. And you could argue that that is the root of the Meninna's hunt, too - the Hosts upset the balance between the Shadow and the material world, and the Beshilu in particular give spirits an easy entrance into the world. Hell, as nofather said, you can easily say that the Iron Masters hunt humans *because* of their effect on the Shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just forgetting all of the personal reasons one could use to justify joining a tribe. Uratha are passionate. If I'm a coroner who opens up a body and rats start to pour out of it like a broken dam and I first-change that very night? that's gonna mark me.<br /> <br /> If you get kidnapped and tortured halfway by the Anshega prior to your change, and still manage to conceive an auspice? Because the fuckers wanted to specifically peel it off with silver and fire? Blood freakin' Talon dude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T09:40:07-07:00","id":153944,"title":"","content":"So, I'm the cad responsible for the intial chunk of rules and background for the Idigam, while other writers like Strider are handling the specific example Idigam that the book will be featuring. I'm happy to go over some of the queries in this thread and field any others that people may have for me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=147138#post147138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stew says they're spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're <i>probably </i>spirits, depending on which (if any) of the possible options we provide is the one you choose for your game. They broadly follow the spirit ruleset but with a number of significant differences. I looked at the rules in Wolfsbane and used those as a basis, but the new Idigam have a fair number of changes - mainly in the powers department.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=147182#post147182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Fenric comparison right on the heels of &quot;they're not cosmic horrors&quot; gives me ample cause to believe Stew when he says that he's sleep-deprived; I can't help but look at the latter as an excuse to talk shit about Lovecraft, which, while not unreasonable, is kind of off-subject. They're ancient shifting monstrosities from before history that truck with mysterious beings from beyond the stars and that's generally enough to ping most people's understanding of the popcultural version of Lovecraft.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not cosmic horror in that they don't reflect a horror viewpoint of a vast, horrible and uncaring universe that you will be crushed by more or less incidentally. The Idigam <i>know</i> the Uratha and they mostly hate them in a way that is very personal and immediate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=147189#post147189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing you didn't got if you read Wolfbane. Color me disappointed.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's quite a few differences to the Wolfsbane ruleset - it was solid enough but I was given a chance to rework it and I wasn't going to pass that up. You'll be getting some more detailed coverage of the differences between Earth-Bound and Moon-Banished, some expansion of the 'life cycle' of the Idigam and a wide suite of new Dread Powers alongside templates to represent the changed and warped servants that the Idigam create.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T09:48:19-07:00","id":153952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=148134#post148134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really subpar previews as a whole if you compare them with the ones done for B&amp;S. Why? Because it's not the writers who do the spoilers, and raise hype on them. Who have actual time to reply to us, address our concerns, and do some revision right there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I can quite happily chat with people and reply about it here in this thread; I would have done so earlier but was in a <i>very</i> muddy field over the Bank Holiday weekend then been busy with work since. Finally have some free time combined with energy!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T10:32:45-07:00","id":153974,"title":"","content":"Earth-Bound and Moon-Banished. This is a delicious teaser.<br /> <br /> Are the Su'ur in affect? Wolfsbane was ambiguous about them, saying the Gurdilag could do it, but the others might not be able to. I suppose using that, it'd be an Earth-bound ability?<br /> <br /> Always nice to have some free time, our group got a ton of gaming in this last three day weekend, it was really refreshing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T10:51:42-07:00","id":154006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's quite a few differences to the Wolfsbane ruleset - it was solid enough but I was given a chance to rework it and I wasn't going to pass that up. You'll be getting some more detailed coverage of the differences between Earth-Bound and Moon-Banished, some expansion of the 'life cycle' of the Idigam and a wide suite of new Dread Powers alongside templates to represent the changed and warped servants that the Idigam create. </div> </div> </div>See? I wouldn't have been nearly so disappointed if this was in the actual blog. This also proves my point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T11:29:21-07:00","id":154056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=153974#post153974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Earth-Bound and Moon-Banished. This is a delicious teaser.<br /> <br /> Are the Su'ur in affect? Wolfsbane was ambiguous about them, saying the Gurdilag could do it, but the others might not be able to. I suppose using that, it'd be an Earth-bound ability?<br /> <br /> Always nice to have some free time, our group got a ton of gaming in this last three day weekend, it was really refreshing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Su'ur are in. The ability to make a specific type of servitor is a given power pick, so an Idigam that can, say, tear the souls out of humans and make them into claimed (or use the souls as weird Twilight minions) won't necessarily be able to make Su'ur, and vice versa. Su'ur themselves are fairly straightforward in nature to make, as templates go, but especially an Idigam with a mixture of Uratha Su'ur and Heralds will be a pretty terrifying opponent to go up against. They are explicitly not just an Earth-Bound thing - I'm pretty sure Gurdilag was a Moon-Banished, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T12:46:06-07:00","id":154110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=154056#post154056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, Su'ur are in. The ability to make a specific type of servitor is a given power pick, so an Idigam that can, say, tear the souls out of humans and make them into claimed (or use the souls as weird Twilight minions) won't necessarily be able to make Su'ur, and vice versa. Su'ur themselves are fairly straightforward in nature to make, as templates go, but especially an Idigam with a mixture of Uratha Su'ur and Heralds will be a pretty terrifying opponent to go up against. They are explicitly not just an Earth-Bound thing - I'm pretty sure Gurdilag was a Moon-Banished, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Moon Banished is Idigam in first tongue. Is there a term for the Earth-Bound in the language of the spirits? if so, which is it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T15:21:39-07:00","id":154220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=153944#post153944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're not cosmic horror in that they don't reflect a horror viewpoint of a vast, horrible and uncaring universe that you will be crushed by more or less incidentally. The Idigam <i>know</i> the Uratha and they mostly hate them in a way that is very personal and immediate.</div> </div> </div> </div>And while I can appreciate that, TVTropes, <span style=\"color:#800080\">shining beacon of words-mean-things that it is</span>, caused and/or amplified a lot of mutation of the term in the public consciousness to be an objective noun interchangeable with &quot;eldritch abomination,&quot; which is in all likelihood what people actually <i>meant</i> when they called the idigam a homonym for a thematic noun signifying big-world-small-you style spookiness.<br /> <br /> This is what I mean when I say it looks like a demonstration of sleep deprivation to throw out the name of an entity whose setting literally refers to it as a Great Old One as an example of what the idigam are like not two breaths after explaining why the narrative of the idigam is not one of cosmic horror in response to what were in all likelihood people misusing the term by describing the idigam as &quot;cosmic horrors.&quot;<br /> <br /> Internet Whisper-Down-The-Lane happens. It is awful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T15:35:19-07:00","id":154226,"title":"","content":"Even if their theme is not exactly cosmic horror and I think the distinction is pretty important, the Idigam could be described literally as &quot;cosmic horrors&quot; if you think about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3058-juvenaliansatyr","name":"JuvenalianSatyr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3058_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T19:14:09-07:00","id":154440,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I get that stew was trying to dispel the association between the Idigam and the works of Lovecraft. But they are pretty literally both cosmic and horror. And they do share more than a few similarities with the eldritch creatures of the cthulu mythos. The themes may be different, but superficially they are difficult to distinguish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T19:20:24-07:00","id":154443,"title":"","content":"Fun fact, cthulu mythos is conan mythos. Set in the same world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T19:29:40-07:00","id":154455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=154443#post154443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fun fact, cthulu mythos is conan mythos. Set in the same world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apropos discussion tidbit from the old Exalted forums:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do find that kind of philosophy entertaining, though. Lovecraft goes out of his way to remind us about how puny and insignificant humanity is compared to these great and mighty beings... and then Howard makes a character that literally beats them to death with his bare hands. [\u2026]</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iozz-Sothoth</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is literally true in the round-robin story The Challenge from Beyond, where Howard's chapter follows Lovecraft's -- our hero suddenly shifts from a state of utter terror in the face of an alien horror to attempting to brain it with a handy electron-microscope. IIRC, he then threatens to kill their god, and by the end of the chapter is their king. I have some sympathy for the poor guy who had to conclude it after that (Frank Belknap Long, I think.)</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T19:41:20-07:00","id":154464,"title":"","content":"In one of the stories Conan does battle with one of the Cthulu old gods or some such. Damn near dies in the encounter but he's so bad ass nothing stops him (never mind the life saving potion the lady of the hour had).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T23:59:53-07:00","id":154599,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the cthulhu mythos has been flanderized over the years, while Lovecraft's writing subjects faint from bad smells, there should still be room for Howard's protagonists who would just make sashimi out of what confronts them too. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T04:17:18-07:00","id":154680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=154110#post154110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Moon Banished is Idigam in first tongue. Is there a term for the Earth-Bound in the language of the spirits? if so, which is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>There isn't currently one in the first draft because I'm still mulling over what to call them. Not sure whether to go with <i>nu-</i><i>idigam </i>- 'not moon-banished' - or <i>gihal-zah</i> or <i>gihal-ennu</i>, both of which more directly mean earth-bound.<br /> <br /> Any opinions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T05:04:48-07:00","id":154706,"title":"","content":"I like the ring of Gihal-zah","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T06:16:34-07:00","id":154751,"title":"","content":"Seconded on that name","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png