occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T10:22:19-07:00","id":154961,"title":"","content":"That just makes me picture the members of GWAR as coalesced Idigam. Which is an idea that I will now be using.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T10:32:29-07:00","id":154974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=154220#post154220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And while I can appreciate that, TVTropes, <span style=\"color:#800080\">shining beacon of words-mean-things that it is</span>, caused and/or amplified a lot of mutation of the term in the public consciousness to be an objective noun interchangeable with &quot;eldritch abomination,&quot; which is in all likelihood what people actually <i>meant</i> when they called the idigam a homonym for a thematic noun signifying big-world-small-you style spookiness.<br /> <br /> This is what I mean when I say it looks like a demonstration of sleep deprivation to throw out the name of an entity whose setting literally refers to it as a Great Old One as an example of what the idigam are like not two breaths after explaining why the narrative of the idigam is not one of cosmic horror in response to what were in all likelihood people misusing the term by describing the idigam as &quot;cosmic horrors.&quot;<br /> <br /> Internet Whisper-Down-The-Lane happens. It is awful.</div> </div> </div> </div>[Ambassador of TV Tropes Rant Incoming]<br /> <br /> And the thing is, it's <i>especially </i>sad if that mutated from TV Tropes, in specific. We <i>specifically say </i>that while the trope &quot;eldritch abomination&quot;, while it's native to Lovecraft, isn't always a part of cosmic horror as a genre, that's an <i>entirely different page. </i>We <i>changed the name </i>from Cosmic Horror to Eldritch Abomination to <i>prevent </i>this exact kind of confusion. &quot;Eldritch Abomination&quot; is simply &quot;a monster defined by its violation of what we consider natural laws&quot;, it does <i>not </i>mean &quot;Lovecraftian god.&quot;<br /> <br /> While the idigam <i>are </i>Eldritch Abominations, they are <i>not </i>characters in a cosmic horror story, and in fact the nWoD itself is defined by the fact that it isn't really an example of the genre. The vast majority of monsters and main antagonists are defined by comprehensible, self-willed motivations like greed or the desire to survive. The closest we get to a true Cthulhu is the God-Machine, and there's an entire <i>game line </i>about it screwing up, and Demon is defined by human-scale stories. Idigam not the least of these, their motivation is a desire to remain free and to avenge their humiliation by Father Wolf on his descendants, both things that are easily understood by humans (as the sign of a massive dick with antiquated views of justice, but understood). More than that, they can be overcome, and each one destroyed is a problem permanently solved, because each one is self-contained. So not the Great Old Ones at all.<br /> <br /> So, to sum up? If that actually is the case, the rumor chain managed to give less meaning to words <i>than TV Tropes.</i><br /> <br /> That's just plain sad.<br /> <br /> [/Rant]<br /> <br /> So, to sum up, I perfectly understand your point and perfectly support it.<br /> <br /> And I perfectly understand why the &quot;this is not Lovecraftian horror, it's normal horror with tentacles&quot; disclaimer had to be done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 05-31-2014, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T11:50:10-07:00","id":155052,"title":"","content":"Mmmm, <i>Gihal-ennu</i> sound more like something a deranged cultist could mutter, I like it best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T04:56:40-07:00","id":155597,"title":"","content":"So, let me think, are there any other tidbits I can spill into the thread without Stew making a new coat out of my skin...<br /> <br /> - Here's one, an admission: I'm not happy with my current draft of the Idigam rules. Stew's probably redlining it at the moment, which will help, but I feel like I can do much better with the coming second draft in emphasising the Idigam themes and tightening &amp; improving their powers.<br /> - Idigam are the big bad for Forsaken. They can be defeated or even bound and imprisoned away, but they can never be mastered or controlled no matter the source of the power. 'Oh, just get a Spirit Mage to deal with it' really isn't an answer to the Idigam threat.<br /> - Some Idigam can acquire souls through various means (like ripping them out of a human then shoving a spirit in); this was mentioned in Wolfsbane but I wanted to elaborate on it a bit, so there are some example powers for just what an Idigam might then <i>do</i> with a human soul.<br /> - There's a Dread Power to help represent the resilience that REALLY BIG Idigam have. Want to do a Kaiju Moon-Banished? Go ahead.<br /> - There's a much longer list of Essence Shaping and Dread Powers than Wolfsbane had, and I sorely wish I had more word count in order to shove even more in there. Thousands of words seem to disappear rather quickly when you're having fun writing...<br /> - The sample Idigam that the other writers have cooked up are really cool <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T08:55:59-07:00","id":155675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=155597#post155597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- The sample Idigam that the other writers have cooked up are really cool <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>In regards to the ones I did....aww, thanks! *blush* <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T11:05:28-07:00","id":155758,"title":"","content":"Don't blush! It's the breeder affecting you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T08:41:43-07:00","id":156553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=155597#post155597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, let me think, are there any other tidbits I can spill into the thread without Stew making a new coat out of my skin...<br /> ...<br /> - There's a Dread Power to help represent the resilience that REALLY BIG Idigam have. Want to do a Kaiju Moon-Banished? Go ahead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I'll most likely never actually run <i>Werewolf</i> or any WoD game where a kaiju spirit-monster would make sense but oh I'll still enjoy this.<br /> <br /> Maybe one other thing about their rules could be spoilered? Spirits are obviously (relatively) straight forward ephemeral entity rules, whereas Strix are as well in their own way. The Idigam corrupt spirits, as mentioned on the blog, but they themselves are spirits of alien places or forgotten, irrelevant concepts, so are they built using ephemeral entity rules? I suppose even in <i>Wolfsbane</i> they have ranks and bans, but I was curious if their expanded concept has warranted a different mechanical execution","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T09:43:07-07:00","id":156613,"title":"","content":"Yes, Idigam are built on ephemeral entity spirit rules with adjustments to fit the nature of the beings in question, so they have things like Ranks, Bans and Banes. However, they also have Essence Shaping and Dread Powers. Completely reinventing the wheel for their rules would, I'm afraid, have thrown me well over my word count!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T09:52:27-07:00","id":156619,"title":"","content":"I'm interested in seeing how the Idigam interact with the God Machine, its Infrastructure and its agents. As for NWoD not having cosmic horror as a theme, I'll just point at the GMC core rules book, mention the obvious Lovecraftian influence (with a bit of Barker for good measure) and walk away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T09:58:11-07:00","id":156628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=156613#post156613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, Idigam are built on ephemeral entity spirit rules with adjustments to fit the nature of the beings in question, so they have things like Ranks, Bans and Banes. However, they also have Essence Shaping and Dread Powers. Completely reinventing the wheel for their rules would, I'm afraid, have thrown me well over my word count!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for answering; it sounds great, actually. Reinventing the rules wasn't what I was hoping for. However strange and alien the Idigam are, their nature doesn't warrant a complete rules rewrite...<br /> <br /> ...right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T10:12:24-07:00","id":156645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=156619#post156619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm interested in seeing how the Idigam interact with the God Machine, its Infrastructure and its agents. As for NWoD not having cosmic horror as a theme, I'll just point at the GMC core rules book, mention the obvious Lovecraftian influence (with a bit of Barker for good measure) and walk away.</div> </div> </div> </div>My plan for the upcoming crossover game I'm going to run once IC comes out is for the Idigam's prison on the moon to have been the Tomb of the Butterfly. They'll actually have been quite heavily influenced by the God-Machine during their imprisonment - not exactly its agents, and certainly not actual angels, but their nature will definitely have been altered by exposure to its influence. Of course, I'm going to be making a lot of wonky God Machine connections in that game. For example, Loci will actually be Occult Matrices that Spirits and werewolves leech essence off of, oblivious to their actual purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T11:03:52-07:00","id":156745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=156619#post156619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm interested in seeing how the Idigam interact with the God Machine, its Infrastructure and its agents. As for NWoD not having cosmic horror as a theme, I'll just point at the GMC core rules book, mention the obvious Lovecraftian influence (with a bit of Barker for good measure) and walk away.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was hoping that like Blood and Smoke, Idigam Chronicle (does it have another title, like Blood and Smoke: The Strix Chronicle do?) would mostly ignore the God Machine, which exists mainly as a plot device for mortal and God Machine games. Certainly it's the type of thing you could put into other games, alongside qashmallim and Exarchs and the Crone, but ideally the Idigam book will put the focus on the werewolves and their issues.<br /> <br /> Also I'm not sure about the thread, but the developers were mainly saying that cosmic horror is not a theme in the idigam, not in the world of darkness at large.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T11:08:57-07:00","id":156747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=156745#post156745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... (does it [the Idigam Chronicle] have another title, like Blood and Smoke: The Strix Chronicle do?) ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at this time. Although The Wolf Must Hunt might be a good one, considering how central that phrase is to the new design direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T11:59:04-07:00","id":156801,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you can probably safely expect the Idigam Chronicle to mostly ignore the God Machine plot element.<br /> <br /> We've already got so much stuff we have to pack into the book just from the Forsaken setting alone :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T13:56:01-07:00","id":156890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/147087-idigam-chronicles-wekly-discussion-moon-banished-idigam?p=156745#post156745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was hoping that like Blood and Smoke, Idigam Chronicle (does it have another title, like Blood and Smoke: The Strix Chronicle do?) would mostly ignore the God Machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I vote for <i><b>Sexy Savagery - The Idigam Chronicles</b></i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span s